    {
      "id": "QR-TB-004",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "category": "correctness-deadline-publication",
      "artifact": "src/dotnet/Vulgata.Web/Data/PreparedChatCoordinator.cs",
      "location": "551-563; src/dotnet/Vulgata.Web/Components/Pages/ChatPage.razor.cs:393-436; src/dotnet/Vulgata.Web/Components/Pages/ChatRevealDelay.cs:8-12",
      "affected_requirement": "AD-7, AD-7B; FR-031, FR-032, FR-056; SC-017; grounded-chat-v2 boundary steps 8-9 and provider-streaming deadline-through-publication/render contract",
      "evidence": "QR-TB-002 is only partially closed. The coordinator checks cancellation before answer construction and before append, but then appends the validated conversation turn, reads the remaining deadline, and unconditionally returns Succeeded even when that final read is zero/negative or has triggered the deadline token. A deterministic TimeProvider can therefore expire at the final remaining-budget read after append and still publish success. The page separately treats every remaining budget of at least 1,000 ms as sufficient for progressive reveal, while production reveal delays 25 ms per Unicode text element and is linked only to caller cancellation; a valid long answer can continue publication beyond the same absolute 29-second budget. Existing deadline tests expire only in retrieval/currentness/advisory reread, and the UI test covers only the fixed 500 ms immediate-render case, so all 381 passing Track B tests miss both publication boundaries.",
      "correction_outcome": "Keep one absolute deadline authoritative through the final append/result boundary and accepted UI publication. Add fake-clock REDs that expire at the final remaining-budget/publication read and prove no success or conversation append, plus a page RED where remaining budget is above 1,000 ms but below the actual reveal cost and prove immediate complete render within budget. Preserve the distinct caller-cancelled versus internal-timeout outcomes and do not weaken accepted-only reveal.",
      "earliest_owner": "implement"
    }
  ],
  "summary": "REVISE with one HIGH finding. QR-TB-001 is closed: the A/B/A race compares reveal state to packet-owned advisory text and authority fingerprint and withholds before answer/citation/conversation publication. QR-TB-003 is closed: only local invalid-JSON syntax carries the bounded 2,048-character response and closed repair category; valid-JSON semantic, handle, fingerprint, evidence, and citation failures do not repair. Packet 2.2, typed one-path retrieval, current-v2 many-decision/Flow Group currentness, strict streaming byte domains/terminal/EOF/inactivity, production raw-adapter composition, content-dark Track B telemetry, authorization, no-migration, Story 12.4, and Track C exclusion checks found no additional blocking defect. Verification passed 381/381 exact Track B tests and the Web build with zero errors; git diff check passed. Known NU1507/NU1900 and EF assembly-version MSB3277 warnings remain. Track C T038-T045/T054-T062 and real provider/PostgreSQL/restart/screenshot/release evidence were not run or accepted. Independent read-only review; no production, test, specification, plan, task, lifecycle-state, staging, commit, or Git-history mutation was performed, and the only write is this verdict artifact."
